### 6. **Session Creation and Budget Integration** (ralph.ts lines 1513–1547)

```typescript
// 1. Create session with optional budget
const sessionId = ulid();
process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION = sessionId;
process.env.KSPEC_SESSION_ID = sessionId;

await createSessionWithBudget(specDir, {
  id: sessionId,
  agent_type: workerAdapterId,
  budget: maxTasks, // 0 = no budget
});

// 2. Inject into per-role adapter configs
const uniqueAdapterIds = [...new Set([
  normalizeForEnv(workerAdapterId),
  normalizeForEnv(reviewerAdapterId),
])];

for (const id of uniqueAdapterIds) {
  const injectionResult = await injectEnvForAdapter(id, sessionId);
  previousEnvValues.set(id, injectionResult?.previousValue);
}

// 3. Log session start event with both adapters
await appendEvent(specDir, {
  session_id: sessionId,
  type: "session.start",
  data: {
    workerAdapter: workerAdapterId,
    reviewerAdapter: reviewerAdapterId,
    maxLoops, maxTasks, yolo, focus, explicitTasks,
  },
});
```

**Key Guarantees:**
- Session created before any events (enables recovery)
- Env injection per unique harness (deduplicates claude-code-acp)
- Signal handlers installed immediately after (so cleanup always runs)
- Budget reset only between iterations (not during agent execution)

---

### 7. **Cleanup Patterns** (ralph.ts finally block, lines 2117+)

```typescript
finally {
  // 1. Remove signal handlers to prevent double cleanup
  process.off("SIGINT", sigintHandler);
  process.off("SIGTERM", sigtermHandler);

  // 2. Dispose spawned agent
  if (agent) {
    sessionUpdateLogger = replaceSessionUpdateLogger(agent.client, sessionUpdateLogger, null);
    acpSessionId = endAcpSession(agent, acpSessionId);
    agent = disposeSpawnedAgent(agent);
  }

  // 3. Delete budget
  await fs.unlink(getSessionBudgetPath(specDir, sessionId)).catch(() => {});

  // 4. Remove env injections per adapter
  for (const id of uniqueAdapterIds) {
    await removeEnvForAdapter(id, previousEnvValues.get(id));
  }

  // 5. Clear session env
  delete process.env.KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION;
  delete process.env.KSPEC_SESSION_ID;

  // 6. Spawn wrap-up agent
  if (!options.dryRun && exitReason) {
    const wrapUpCtx = buildWrapUpContext(exitReason, ...);
    const wrapUpResult = await runWrapUpAgent(workerAdapter, wrapUpCtx, ...);
    await appendEvent(...);
  }

  // 7. Close session
  // [In signal handlers, done synchronously via async IIFE]
  await closeSession(specDir, sessionId, "completed", "Loop completed normally");
}
```

**Signal Handler Strategy:**
- SIGINT/SIGTERM trigger async IIFE (keeps event loop alive)
- Cleans up agent, env, budget sequentially
- Calls process.exit(0) after cleanup (no error exit code)
- Prevents double cleanup by removing handlers in finally

