### 10. **Skill Resolution and Invocation**

**Skill Origins Loading:**
```typescript
async function loadSkillOriginsForRalph(ctx: KspecContext): Promise<Map<string, SkillOrigin>>
```
- Reads skill metadata (core vs project)
- Provides fallback for core skills not in meta

**Platform-Aware Invocation Resolution:**
```typescript
function resolveRalphSkillInvocation(
  invocation: string,  // "{skill:task-work}" or "/kspec:task-work" or "$kspec-task-work"
  platform: RalphPromptPlatform,  // "claude-code" | "codex" | "unknown"
  skillOrigins: Map<string, SkillOrigin>,
): string
```
- Converts between platforms: `/kspec:X` ↔ `$kspec-X` (codex style)
- Resolves `{skill:X}` tokens to platform-appropriate syntax

---

### 11. **Explicit Task Scope in Prompts**

When --tasks is set, the task-work prompt includes:
```markdown
## Explicit Task Scope

This session is scoped to specific tasks: @task1, @task2

**Only work on these tasks.** The loop will exit when all listed tasks are completed or blocked.
```

The mode description changes:
```
Loop mode means: no confirmations, auto-resolve decisions, explicit task scope (only the listed tasks).
```

Instead of:
```
Loop mode means: no confirmations, auto-resolve decisions, automation-eligible tasks only.
```

---

### 12. **Key Integration Points**

| Component | How Ralph Uses It | Critical Detail |
|-----------|------------------|-----------------|
| **spawnAndInitialize** | Per-worker adapter, once per run (or restart) | Initializes ACP handshake, captures capabilities |
| **appendEvent** | Per iteration (prompts, timeouts, results) | Atomic writes, auto-seq, optional externalization |
| **injectEnvForAdapter** | Before loop, per unique adapter | Deduplicates claude-code-acp aliases |
| **resetBudget** | At iteration start | No-op if no budget configured |
| **createSessionUpdateLogger** | Per ACP session (one per iteration) | Replaces logger between iterations to prevent cross-iteration leakage |
| **handleIterationFailure** | After iteration fails, tracks per-task | Escalates at 3 consecutive failures |
| **processPendingReviewTasks** | After context gathered, before main iteration | Subagent sequencing, timeout/status handling |
| **closeSession** | In signal handler + finally | Records close_reason (abandoned, completed, etc.) |

